  "identifier": "apex-switch-sunset-2026",
  "headline": "Apex Legends ends Nintendo Switch support on August 4, 2026",
  "description": "Respawn will sunset Apex Legends on Nintendo Switch on August 4, 2026. Season 29 is the final update for the original Switch, while Season 30 and ongoing support continue on other platforms including Switch 2.",
  "articleBody": "Respawn Entertainment announced that Apex Legends will stop operating on Nintendo Switch on August 4, 2026. Players can continue to play until that date, but the platform will no longer receive new updates or content beyond the final Switch season.\n\nSeason 29 will be the last update for the original Switch version. Starting with Season 30 on August 4, Apex Legends will remain available on other platforms, including Nintendo Switch 2.\n\nThe publisher noted that cross-progression ties items and account progress to EA accounts, allowing players to carry their cosmetics and purchases to supported platforms when they switch hardware.",
